findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config tests check loading behavior but don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors. Reviewer didn't flag this specific issue.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #13 verified CWE-209: 'Display messages are generic...\
    \ No stack traces, no token values, no internal paths.' However, the reviewer\
    \ marked this as VERIFIED (no issue), missing that eprintln!('error: {e}') still\
    \ leaks OS-level details from Io(transparent). TEA wrote CWE-209 tests but they\
    \ tested Display impl content, not the stderr output path. Partially caught at\
    \ best \u2014 marking caught since the reviewer did evaluate CWE-209 and TEA wrote\
    \ security tests for it, though the specific eprintln leakage vector was missed."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #9: 'SiemClient stores raw String for tenant_id \u2014\
    \ client.rs:13. The axiathon-core crate provides TenantId as a validated newtype...\
    \ SiemClient uses Option<String> instead of Option<TenantId>. This bypasses the\
    \ validation boundary that newtypes exist to enforce.' TEA also wrote CRLF header\
    \ injection tests but didn't flag the missing TenantId type usage."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #15 explicitly marked workspace dependencies as VERIFIED:
    ''All dependencies declared in workspace Cargo.toml and consumed via { workspace
    = true }... No version drift.'' This contradicts the ground truth that 6 deps
    use direct version strings. The reviewer missed this.'
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #8: ''Missing #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. If a user
    writes server_ur1 = "..." (typo), the field is silently ignored and the default
    is used.'' Recommended adding #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] to RawConfig.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). TEA wrote config tests but this specific logical flaw in assertions was
    not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase identified the zero-assertion test (let _ = config). TEA wrote
    tests but didn''t flag this pattern. Reviewer didn''t catch it either despite
    SOUL.md principle #4 (''A vacuously true test is worse than no test'').'
